"""Frozen H-039 R23/R14 populated-FD and fixed-helper upgrade gate.

No arguments execute pre-product RED while authenticating the published R11
product, the owner-witnessed partial state, and the exact directory-cursor
failure. The installer selects the corrected function while runtime compilation
selects the exact historical function. Historical lanes remain frozen. Distinct ``--r19-product`` and
``--r19-published`` lanes bind one cursor-independent R12 installer and current
live publication. R22 consumes the single owner-authorized INT2 zero-effect
observation and admits only a compile-time, no-output pre-store diagnostic.
R23 consumes the owner-adjudicated, zero-effect R22/R13 status-28 lifecycle,
keeps that historical diagnostic branch byte-exact, and admits only the exact
R12-to-R14 fixed-object update plus the populated second FD inventory.  This
Python gate never runs elevated, installs anything, or accepts a cleanup path,
PID, command, or caller-selected descriptor.
"""

